 S('Namaste! Subnetting ka matlab hai ek bade network ko chhote chhote networks mein todna. Analogy: ek badi colony hai, usse tum gali number ek, do, teen mein baant dete ho. Har gali ek subnet hai. Subnetting mein hum host ke kuch bits udhaar lete hain subnet banane ke liye. Agar n bits udhaar liye to two to the power n subnets milte hain.',
  'Subnet = colony ki galiyan. n bits udhaar = 2^n subnets',
  [['h', 'Borrow bits from host part'], ['row', ['Network 24 bits', 'Subnet n bits', 'Host h bits']], ['t', 'n + h = 8 (for a Class C network).'], ['tbl', [['Borrow n', 'Subnets 2^n', 'Hosts 2^h-2'], ['1', '2', '126'], ['2', '4', '62'], ['3', '8', '30'], ['4', '16', '14'], ['5', '32', '6']]]],
  ['## Formulas', 'Subnets = 2^n', 'Hosts = 2^h - 2', 'Block size = 2^h', '~ -2 = network + broadcast', '## Quick check', 'n = 3 -> h = 5', 'hosts = 2^5 - 2 = 30', '! 8 subnets, 30 hosts each']),
 S('Ab exam ka question. Organization ko block mila hai two eleven dot seventeen dot one eighty dot zero slash twenty-four. Administrator ko battis subnets chahiye. Pehla sawaal, subnet mask kya hoga. Battis barabar two to the power paanch, to n barabar paanch. Prefix twenty-four plus paanch barabar twenty-nine. Mask ke last octet mein paanch aur teen zero, yaani one one one one one zero zero zero, jo do sau aThatalis hota hai.',
  '32 subnets -> n = 5 -> /29 -> 255.255.255.248',
  [['h', 'Q: 211.17.180.0/24, need 32 subnets'], ['bits', '11111000', ['1', '1', '1', '1', '1', '0', '0', '0']], ['t', 'Last octet mask = 1111 1000 = 248'], ['t', 'Block size = 256 - 248 = 8']],
  ['## Find the mask', '32 = 2^5 -> n = 5', 'prefix = 24 + 5 = 29', 'last octet: 11111000', '128+64+32+16+8 = 248', '! Mask = 255.255.255.248 (/29)', '## Block and hosts', 'h = 8 - 5 = 3', 'block = 2^3 = 8', 'hosts = 8 - 2 = 6']),
 S('Dusra sawaal: subnet number battis ka pehla aur aakhri address. Subnets zero se shuru hote hain, to subnet battis ka index hai ekattis. Har block ka size aath hai. To start address barabar ekattis into aath, yaani do sau aThatalis. Subnet ek: two eleven dot seventeen dot one eighty dot two forty-eight. Aakhri address start plus saat, yaani two fifty-five.',
  'Last subnet start = (32 - 1) x 8 = 248',
  [['h', 'First and last address of subnet 32'], ['tbl', [['Subnet', 'First', 'Last'], ['1', '.0', '.7'], ['2', '.8', '.15'], ['...', '...', '...'], ['32', '.248', '.255']]]],
  ['## Subnet 32', 'index = 32 - 1 = 31', 'start = 31 x 8 = 248', 'end = 248 + 8 - 1 = 255', '! First: 211.17.180.248/29', '! Last : 211.17.180.255/29', '~ Usable hosts: .249 to .254']),
 S('Ab sabse common numerical: ek IP diya hai aur network address, broadcast address, hosts nikaalne hain. IP one seventy-two dot sixteen dot thirty-five dot one thirty slash twenty-six. Slash twenty-six ka mask do fifty-five dot do fifty-five dot do fifty-five dot one ninety-two. Block size two fifty-six minus one ninety-two barabar sixty-four. Blocks hain zero, sixty-four, one twenty-eight, one ninety-two. Ek tirees mein one thirty one twenty-eight aur one ninety-one ke beech aata hai.',
  'Block size nikalo, phir dekho IP kis block mein hai',
  [['h', 'Q: 172.16.35.130 / 26'], ['row', ['0 - 63', '64 - 127', '128 - 191', '192 - 255']], ['t', '130 falls in the third block (128 - 191).']],
  ['## Step 1: mask', '/26 -> 255.255.255.192', '## Step 2: block', '256 - 192 = 64', '## Step 3: find block of 130', '128 <= 130 <= 191', '! Network  : 172.16.35.128', '! Broadcast: 172.16.35.191', '! Usable   : .129 to .190', 'Hosts = 2^6 - 2 = 62']),
 S('Last mein do chhote numericals. Pehla: mask do fifty-five dot do fifty-five dot do forty dot zero ka prefix kya hai. Do fifty-five matlab aath ones, do baar, sixteen. Do forty matlab one one one one zero zero zero zero, yaani chaar ones. Total twenty. Host bits barah, to hosts two to the power barah minus two barabar chaar hazaar ninety-four. Dusra: kya do IP ek hi subnet mein hain? AND karke dekho.',
  'Mask to prefix: ones ginte jao. Same subnet: AND karo',
  [['h', 'Mask <-> prefix'], ['tbl', [['Octet', 'Binary', 'Ones'], ['255', '1111 1111', '8'], ['240', '1111 0000', '4'], ['224', '1110 0000', '3'], ['192', '1100 0000', '2']]]],
  ['## Q: 255.255.240.0 -> prefix', '8 + 8 + 4 + 0 = 20', 'host bits = 32 - 20 = 12', '! /20, hosts = 2^12 - 2 = 4094', '## Q: same subnet? /27', '192.168.1.40 and 192.168.1.60', 'block = 256 - 224 = 32', '40 and 60 are both in 32 - 63', '! YES, same subnet']),
